  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "If I keep moving, they won't know |\r\nI'll morph to someone else |\r\nWhat they throw at me's too slow |\r\nI'll morph to someone else |\r\nI'm just a ghost |\r\nI'll morph to someone else |\r\nDefense mechanism mode!\n\nYou are given two integer sequences A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ and B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​ and an integer KKK. You may perform the following operation at most 3⋅N3 \\cdot N3⋅N times:\n\n\nSelect a contiguous subsequence of AAA with length KKK. Let's denote this subsequence by AL,AL+1,…,AL+K−1A_L, A_{L+1}, \\ldots, A_{L+K-1}AL​,AL+1​,…,AL+K−1​.\nCreate an integer sequence S1,S2,…,SKS_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_KS1​,S2​,…,SK​ which is isomorphic to the selected subsequence ― for each pair of integers iii and jjj (1≤i,j≤K1 \\le i, j \\le K1≤i,j≤K), Si=SjS_i = S_jSi​=Sj​ must hold if AL−1+i=AL−1+jA_{L-1+i} = A_{L-1+j}AL−1+i​=AL−1+j​ and Si≠SjS_i \\neq S_jSi​=Sj​ must hold if AL−1+i≠AL−1+jA_{L-1+i} \\neq A_{L-1+j}AL−1+i​=AL−1+j​. In addition, 1≤Si≤1,0001 \\le S_i \\le 1,0001≤Si​≤1,000 must hold for each valid iii.\nFor each valid iii, replace AL−1+iA_{L-1+i}AL−1+i​ by SiS_iSi​.\nIs it possible to change the sequence AAA to BBB? If it is possible, find a sequence of operations which morphs AAA to BBB.",
